{"title":"Newton's Inequality","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Background\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Background</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Background\">Background</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Background\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34035ac1de5eb5a76e4d796381ecedd639210f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\ldots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"11\" />, we define the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetric_sum\" title=\"Symmetric sum\">symmetric sum</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdc028050428615cc28ee3c1f9a67eda8e9a726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> to be the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/9200a411ff18fb2d7ee603dd81c19b2cef42ac05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t^{n-k}$\" width=\"32\" height=\"15\" /> in the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f500f67d7c5ef0027979670826bcda86f216078c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\prod_{i=1}^{n}(t+x_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"80\" height=\"48\" /> (see <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Viete%27s_sums\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Viete&#39;s sums\">Viete's sums</a>).  We define the <i>symmetric average</i> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d09bd8dc83be3b4a1bc205b9cc6fa40b23c7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/15901b2963df2aa1eafea0dad31d0d37662a8f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textstyle s_k/{n \\choose k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"47\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d34035ac1de5eb5a76e4d796381ecedd639210f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\ldots, x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/1/911ce44797097cd8927375a6042612693adc02f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; k &lt; n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"78\" height=\"13\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b779dca0af5e2d9824d092daccd6a9c44df615f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k^2 \\ge d_{k-1}d_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>with equality exactly when all the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are equal.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma.</b>\nFor real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c800af561b2321f677f96d4151bbda03a833c35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 , \\ldots, x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"11\" />, there exist real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011fb30f0a62bb5ca1efdc59130946758ed5c1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;_1, \\ldots, x&#39;_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> with the same symmetric averages <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/0/da0c3e837f2bb68444dda5133969b10607c537ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_0, \\ldots, d_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><i>Proof.</i>\nWe consider the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e24c411c4d6c11eeb22714f45db173c3677cfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(t) = \\prod_{i=1}^m (t+x_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"139\" height=\"48\" />.  The roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e74680729d32a37f4ca3b6619446be95325091.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-x_1, \\ldots, -x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"16\" />.  Without loss of generality, we assume that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> increase as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> increases.  Now for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a535b2573c914e1f01dd14806c96c059005f033a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\{1, m-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70fcbb838e7c83cf187c47cc2c971eecaebaa246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> must have a root between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/c/b5c170dc53fce7452e6f7df461222672d913e34e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rolle%27s_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rolle&#39;s theorem\">Rolle's theorem</a> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/56734148d858c16a9a4506cc0551c3bab53eadd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i \\neq x_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"17\" />, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d72b5e495aa2a4697cd4a22e83dcd7ba7f59fe88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = x_{i+1} = \\cdots = x_{i+k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/7/837682bc6103a4c6740c8273434e1a2c771a2514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> is a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/5/f05f085f774fc8ab50676b778b86a1f1d1114fc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> times, so it must be a root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> times.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96eec32de93b032b6d531a03aa5b346156b62a75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"46\" height=\"12\" /> non-positive, real roots, i.e., for some non-negative reals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011fb30f0a62bb5ca1efdc59130946758ed5c1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;_1, \\ldots, x&#39;_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" />,\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/473088396e4c4c76b06dfcbb9a408b31de674dc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${} P&#39;(t) = m \\prod_{i=1}^{m-1}(t+x&#39;_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"169\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>It follows that the symmetric sum <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b4d496fe69bcd007f039a0e4ddbe36358d2dd9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&#39;_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/011fb30f0a62bb5ca1efdc59130946758ed5c1f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&#39;_1, \\ldots, x&#39;_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/0/540ba1240cb4e2bd2520a843d6d7a3bf57e7e8cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m-k}{m}s_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"67\" height=\"37\" />, so the symmetric average <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68fd31c3b27cf69fafa6eac2e7e598d1ce82aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&#39;_k = \\frac{s&#39;_k}{{m-1 \\choose k}} = \\frac{m-k}{m} \\cdot \\frac{s_k}{{m-1 \\choose k}} = \\frac{s_k}{{m \\choose k}} = d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"330\" height=\"47\" />.\n</p><p>Thus to prove Newton's theorem, it is sufficient to prove\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6ed32b27bc7912e3fe70f9ec53d7bc544895712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_{n-1}^2 \\ge d_{n-2}d_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"19\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2fd3971bb77911064c4b85b7adfb899c4bcbf79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_n=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"17\" />, we are done. Otherwise, divide by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/f/e8f08b45431fe8ce8b299492f3c7cc8033eac1fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"21\" />. The inequality then becomes\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9bcad33ac1c38f17abe5bdb656ad18a235453ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{x_i} \\right)^2 \\ge 2n \\sum_{0\\le i&lt;j \\le n} \\frac{1}{x_ix_j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"290\" height=\"61\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>Expanding the left side, we see that this is\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/5/4559ab700055f2f082b9e1ca9517f1c625a5841c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-1)\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{1}{x_i^2}  + (n-1)\\sum_{0\\le i&lt;j \\le n}\\frac{2}{x_ix_j} \\ge 2n \\sum_{0\\le i&lt;j \\le n} \\frac{1}{x_ix_j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"431\" height=\"50\" />.\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>But this is clearly equivalent to\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/d/52db41fcff447b8c6e53c1b0ba104ddaa1dd2413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{\\rm sym}\\frac{1}{x_1^2} \\ge \\sum_{\\rm sym}\\frac{1}{x_1x_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"141\" height=\"47\" />,\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>which holds by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rearrangement_inequality\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Rearrangement inequality\">rearrangement inequality</a>.\n</p><p><i>Proof: without calculus for non-negative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /></i>\n</p><p>We will proceed by induction on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc35b71800f855d1719430aa55eb8a996e3972f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n =2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the inequality just reduces to AM-GM inequality.\nNow suppose that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/e/eaeee057cc98283a5ba2f277ca3ac38f0414f81d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n =m-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"12\" /> some positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/8/b58b5d807ceb003b35866cff36acdbb8dbef22e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\ge 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />    the inequality holds.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7d010bbff66a0c41e43310a51efbaa6bf63396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/a/fcaeea91c5bea53f0f7fb9dc6300816e6320b58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"22\" height=\"10\" /> be non-negative numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d09bd8dc83be3b4a1bc205b9cc6fa40b23c7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> be the symmetric averages of them.\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fc95ede5a1925b2d4e9274f782e44470fda9d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d&#39;_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the symmetric averages of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/ccada11db7b2b90693e2fac4f887a57fce6f96bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3958e984d2597b35da7975f4503cdcf965a777f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ldots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5dc68191ed35b0b92df3e0393548b20effd8eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{m-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"38\" height=\"10\" />.\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/1/9f1f715fd5d143677a492b477b38cd94941973de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k = \\frac{n-k}{n} {d&#39;}_k + \\frac{k}{n} {d&#39;}_{k-1} x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"209\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/1/511db5631b01a415a03018f2f1b41d653d8dfee3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_{k-1}d_{k+1} = \\left(\\frac{n-k+1}{n} {d&#39;}_{k-1} + \\frac{k-1}{n} {d&#39;}_{k-2} x_m \\right)\\left(\\frac{n-k-1}{n} {d&#39;}_{k+1} + \\frac{k+1}{n} {d&#39;}_k x_m \\right)\\]\" width=\"622\" height=\"43\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/f/d0f3d518ccf2eb21c99f0b3035485547e05bfb27.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{(n-k+1)(n-k-1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}{d&#39;}_{k+1} + \\frac{(k-1)(n-k-1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-2} {d&#39;}_{k+1} x_m\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbfbc78b95bea12dd5428438755b8c0c132e900a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[+ \\frac{(n-k+1)(k+1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}{d&#39;}_k x_m + \\frac{(k-1)(k+1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-2}{d&#39;}_k x_m^2\\]\" width=\"466\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/4/dd40cbb0dbd7ab91c76db64f82a642f36026bad3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\le  \\frac{(n-k+1)(n-k-1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_k^2 + \\frac{(k-1)(n-k-1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-2} {d&#39;}_{k+1} x_m\\]\" width=\"484\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6394f025db73c866a5ffe21ad599f13ca9ef0420.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[+ \\frac{(n-k+1)(k+1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}{d&#39;}_k x_m + \\frac{(k-1)(k+1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}^2 x_m^2\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/d/98d969802a07cfc859c003203e0ea4564d0d660c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\le  \\frac{(n-k+1)(n-k-1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_k^2 + \\frac{(k-1)(n-k-1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1} {d&#39;}_{k} x_m\\]\" width=\"475\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6394f025db73c866a5ffe21ad599f13ca9ef0420.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[+ \\frac{(n-k+1)(k+1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}{d&#39;}_k x_m + \\frac{(k-1)(k+1)}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}^2 x_m^2\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/9/78918d4faf1158b0a7cca1863b70d933e3d1217d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\frac{(n-k)^2}{n^2} {d&#39;}_k^2 + \\frac{2(n-k)k}{n^2} {d&#39;}_k {d&#39;}_{k-1} x_m +\\frac{k^2}{n^2} {d&#39;}_{k-1}^2 x_m^2 - \\left(\\frac{d_k}{n} - \\frac{d_{k-1}x_m}{n}\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"539\" height=\"46\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a0dbee07f5029fff428ee04f833241ac57c6c44.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\le  \\left(\\frac{n-k}{n} {d&#39;}_k + \\frac{k}{n} {d&#39;}_{k-1} x_m \\right)^2        = d_k^2\\]\" width=\"261\" height=\"46\" />\nBy induction this completes the proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Newton%27s_Inequality&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Inequality\" title=\"Inequality\">Inequality</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maclaurin%27s_Inequality\" title=\"Maclaurin&#39;s Inequality\">Maclaurin's Inequality</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101302\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 356/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13443/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4856:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018101302 and revision id 243169. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}